# Who has to approve a pull request before it can merge, once branch protection (see
# scripts/setup-branch-protection.sh) turns "Require review from Code Owners" on. GitHub then
# auto-requests these people/teams and blocks merging without their approval - for a brand-new
# plugin listing and for a one-line re-pin alike, because both are pull requests that touch a
# path below.
#
# Replace these placeholder teams with real ones in the five-more-minutes GitHub organisation
# before relying on this file - a handle CODEOWNERS can't resolve to an org member is silently
# ignored by GitHub, not an error, so a wrong name here would quietly turn the gate off.

# Default: anything not matched more specifically still needs a maintainer.
*                                       @five-more-minutes/maintainers

# A plugin listing, new or updated: reviewed against docs/review-checklist.md. This is the path
# a community contributor's pull request actually touches.
/plugins/                              @five-more-minutes/plugin-reviewers

# The example projects offered as starters.
/templates/                            @five-more-minutes/plugin-reviewers

# Everything that decides what "valid" and "verified" mean, or how a listing is checked and
# published - a narrower, more senior review than an individual listing needs, since a mistake
# here can affect every plugin at once.
/verified-owners.json                  @five-more-minutes/maintainers
/schema/                               @five-more-minutes/maintainers
/scripts/                              @five-more-minutes/maintainers
/.github/                              @five-more-minutes/maintainers
